      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:28:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`(apply iappend …)` hits the argument limit. `iconcatenate` of 10,000 one-element ilists raises \"too many arguments to fit in this stack segment\", and so does `iappend-map` (406) over 10,000 elements. SRFI 1\u0027s `concatenate`/`append-map` here handle that size. The SRFI gives `iconcatenate` exactly for lists too long for `apply`, and the commit says long ilists are as safe as long lists.\n\nLoop instead: start from the last ilist and `%rev-onto` the reversed earlier ones. `%map-results` already returns results last-first, so `iappend-map` can share the loop.",
      "revId": "67466ad6527d84b5b1e1c52b96cb79bb4cc0586d",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
