      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed in PS2: `(\u003d? c 1 2)` and `(\u003d? c (ipair 1 2) (ipair 1 3))` are now #f, an ipair sorts before 5, and 1 and 2 hash differently. It follows the SRFI\u0027s order (the empty list, then ipairs, then everything else). Over 13 mixed objects, exactly one of \u003c, \u003d and \u003e holds for every pair, \u003c is transitive, and equal objects hash alike.",
      "parentUuid": "7868565d_abcca187",
      "revId": "67466ad6527d84b5b1e1c52b96cb79bb4cc0586d",
